253
00:16:38,373 --> 00:16:39,700
I want some cash today!

254
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:41,551
Next round's on me, okay?

255
00:16:42,060 --> 00:16:44,440
Bring it, Belt! Let's go!

256
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,840
You got it.

257
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:54,880
Carlyfa, you hussy!

258
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,800
That skirt is way too short!

259
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:00,780
Hey, give it a rest, Polly.

260
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,726
If you don't like it,
don't look at her, okay?

261
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,320
After all this time, why?

262
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,140
Sorry, Polly.

263
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:21,800
Our friendship is over.

264
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,380
I have to eliminate you.

265
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,837
Lucci, no, don't!

266
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,750
You jerk!

267
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:30,320
Leave him alone!

268
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:38,060
Come go!

269
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,140
I embody... Gotland!

270
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,780
What the?

271
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,332
That didn't work at all.

272
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,840
You're nothing but a pest, Shave.

273
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:04,180
He's gone!

274
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,560
Finger pistol.

275
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:38,877
If you weren't made out of rubber,
you'd be dead with a hole in your neck.

276
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:39,790
Lucky you.

277
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,980
You're protecting him, but why?

278
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,140
Why not?

279
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,337
Because I don't want you to kill him!

280
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:03,917
You guys were all friends
just the other day.

281
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,294
How could you do this?

282
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:09,460
We were.

283
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:12,420
Now, things have changed.

284
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,080
It doesn't matter.

285
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,597
You can say what you want.

286
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,268
You're a bunch of traitors.

287
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:19,880
The point is, you're my enemy now.

288
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,497
I made a promise with
Polly to beat the crap

289
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:26,051
out of anybody who tries to hurt Ice Pops.

290
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:28,330
I see.

291
00:19:28,413 --> 00:19:32,100
You decided to trust him
over us, huh? That's right.

292
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:34,967
Because you guys took
away one of my friends.

293
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:36,700
Hey, Robin, what gives?

294
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,457
Why are you acting like this?

295
00:19:38,540 --> 00:19:41,599
If you want to leave the
crew, at least tell me why.

296
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:45,917
Yeah, and why would you want to team up
with people from the world government?

297
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:46,830
That's crazy.

298
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:49,280
Do I have to repeat myself?

299
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:53,357
I believe I said my farewells to the
cook and the doctor before I left.

300
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,017
Didn't you pass that along, Chopper?

301
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:58,917
Of course I did, but just because I
heard it doesn't mean I accept it.

302
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,360
How could you do this?

303
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,020
I did it to make my wish come true.

304
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,957
A wish that can't happen
as long as we're together.

305
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,393
And if you can't accept that, I'm sorry.

306
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:14,660
You may not find it fair, but to accomplish
my goal, I'll make any sacrifice.

307
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:17,020
I see.

308
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:20,697
And that includes framing your own
crewmates for attempted murder.

309
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:22,740
So what is this wish of yours?

310
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,136
I don't have to answer that question.

311
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,731
Are you out of your mind?

312
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:28,840
Wake up, Robin.

313
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:32,060
You have no right to do this.

314
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:34,517
I don't care what it is
you're trying to accomplish.

315
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,117
The consequences are far too great.

316
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:37,360
I've heard enough.

317
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,736
This is no longer your choice to make

318
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:42,760
This should shut you up?

319
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,340
No iceberg!

320
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:51,800
I won't let anyone get in my way.

321
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:13,311
Nothing you're saying is making any sense!

322
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:15,185
You expect me to believe this?

323
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:18,460
Robin, what happened to you?

324
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,612
You're our friend, Rice!

325
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,140
Please, Robin, come back!

326
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:35,426
Sorry to break up the reunion,
but I'll have to stop you there.

327
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:40,697
You see, we have a date this evening
with a very important individual,

328
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:43,017
one that's been over
four years in the making.

329
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,276
We're finished here.

330
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:48,180
In other words, that means
we're finished with you as well.

331
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:55,180
Khalifa, how much time is left?

332
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:57,320
Two minutes.

333
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:58,760
Here's the deal.

334
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:01,437
I know this is sudden, but in two minutes,

335
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:04,108
this building will go
up in a ball of flame.

336
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,520
You're kidding!

337
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:09,060
Of course not.

338
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:12,949
Fire is an effective tool for
erasing all sorts of evidence.

339
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,977
If you don't want to be burned alive,

340
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:18,178
I suggest you leave the
building as soon as possible.

341
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:19,840
Well, I say that.

342
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:26,300
But I have no intention of letting you go.

343
00:22:31,700 --> 00:22:34,177
Looks like it's gonna
be us against them and

344
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:36,920
our friend Robin has
clearly picked her side

345
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:41,060
Luffy Robin is not one of us anymore.

346
00:22:41,180 --> 00:22:42,820
Do you accept that now?

347
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:48,580
No, no way.

348
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:55,177
So noisy anyway, the first
floor is about to set fire!

349
00:22:55,260 --> 00:22:56,417
It won't be pretty!

350
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:59,517
But to be fair, the
culprits are just pirates.

351
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:02,097
You can't expect them to be subtle!

352
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,537
You bastards!

353
00:23:03,620 --> 00:23:08,917
That's nice of you to give us

354
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,557
credit for your attempted arson!

355
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,177
But I think that I'll pass!

356
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:15,817
What's one more crime when we're
going to execute you anyway?

357
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:21,297
Well,

358
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:25,317
I suppose I'll take my leave now!

359
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:27,677
You've done exactly as you were told!

360
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,817
Good work!

361
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:29,977
Robin!

362
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:30,890
Don't go!

363
00:23:30,973 --> 00:23:32,637
You're still one of us!

364
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:34,300
This is farewell.

365
00:23:35,060 --> 00:23:35,890
Robin!

366
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:40,720
Stop her...

367
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,060
...Straw Hat.

368
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,540
We finally found you!

369
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:48,700
I won't let you run away again!

370
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:50,180
Out of my way!

371
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:51,460
Iron buddy.

372
00:23:58,580 --> 00:24:02,420
How come nothing I do to
these guys even phases them?

373
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:05,100
In addition to our offensive techniques,

374
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:07,437
our training has also given us the ability

375
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:10,060
to make our body as solid as an iron wall.

376
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:14,060
Of course, your punches
are weak to begin with.

377
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:15,280
Okay, whatever!

378
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:17,820
I said out of my way!

379
00:24:18,180 --> 00:24:19,420
Paper of art.

380
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:32,620
Even though he's big, he sure is fast!

381
00:24:32,860 --> 00:24:35,331
He's moving like his body's made of paper!

382
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:40,030
Oh no!

383
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,530
Robin!

384
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:47,110
Move it!

385
00:24:47,193 --> 00:24:48,940
Come on!

386
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,230
Pistol!

387
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:53,310
Shave.

388
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:55,980
He disappeared!

389
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:03,320
My legs are so strong that I can
move faster than your eyes can see.

390
00:25:05,740 --> 00:25:06,570
Moonwalk.

391
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:10,180
In fact, I can even leap
off of the air itself.

392
00:25:12,660 --> 00:25:13,860
He's flying!

393
00:25:17,180 --> 00:25:18,680
Ten-best... kick!

394
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:27,480
A slashing attack? Get down! Hurry! Why?

395
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:42,930
Luffy!

396
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:46,477
They did all that with a single kick?

397
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,390
No way!

398
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:50,957
Technically, it was the sharp
gust of wind that followed it.

399
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:53,140
We call it the Tempest Kick.

400
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:02,740
We met on your ship, didn't we, Roronoa?

401
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:08,260
You said you people
aren't real shipwrights.

402
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:12,266
So does that mean you
lied about the Mary Two?

403
00:26:13,460 --> 00:26:14,437
Unfortunately not.

404
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:16,940
I was quite honest about my assessment.

405
00:26:18,380 --> 00:26:20,100
I'm sorry to hear that.

406
00:26:36,460 --> 00:26:37,880
Don't go, Robin!

407
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:40,980
We're not done talking yet!

408
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,320
No, it's over.

409
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:48,100
This is the last time you'll see me Robin

410
00:26:58,380 --> 00:26:59,917
Movie go after Robin.

411
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:00,830
Whatever happens.

412
00:27:00,913 --> 00:27:02,094
Don't let her get away

413
00:27:10,820 --> 00:27:11,740
Confident, huh?

414
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:14,826
You really shouldn't
take your eyes off of me.

415
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:19,910
Zara!

416
00:27:23,300 --> 00:27:24,460
Finger pistol.

417
00:27:28,900 --> 00:27:32,371
It turns out there are some
things more deadly than bullets

418
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,620
What's your problem?

419
00:27:39,060 --> 00:27:41,080
Get out of my way.

420
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,647
All those punches and
he's not even blinking!

421
00:27:44,940 --> 00:27:46,800
I have him, now go.

422
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:56,880
Ryan!

423
00:28:17,460 --> 00:28:19,100
Luffy! Sorrel!

424
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:31,137
I don't believe it how
can they be so strong

425
00:28:31,220 --> 00:28:34,840
I knew you were tough but this is too much

426
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:40,497
We're not like you as
members of CP9 for as long

427
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:44,257
as we can remember we've
trained to surpass the

428
00:28:44,340 --> 00:28:47,877
limits of the human body
and vowed to hone those

429
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,660
skills into an instrument
of absolute justice

430
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:56,282
The results of that training are the
superhuman techniques known as the Six Powers.

431
00:28:57,620 --> 00:29:00,877
So now I'm sure it's
abundantly clear to you why the

432
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:03,901
four of us are the
government's most elite agents.

433
00:29:04,340 --> 00:29:05,817
And by the same token,

434
00:29:05,900 --> 00:29:10,520
you must also realize how miserably
weak a band of pirates is in comparison.

435
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:23,100
Of course, the full extent of our
powers is strictly classified.

436
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:27,220
But rest assured, scum like
you would never make the cut.

437
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:34,080
Lucci, the ignition device
is about to detonate.

438
00:29:34,380 --> 00:29:35,851
We should probably hurry.

439
00:29:36,720 --> 00:29:39,497
But a chance like this one is quite rare.

440
00:29:39,580 --> 00:29:42,060
Let me show you something interesting.

441
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:46,440
Devil Fruit powers!

442
00:29:48,280 --> 00:29:49,980
Which one is it?

443
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:02,257
Lucci, what in the...?

444
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:04,320
Cat-cat fruit.

445
00:30:08,400 --> 00:30:10,500
The leopard model

446
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:18,440
A human leopard He's
huge What's going on here

447
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:22,300
What in the hell are you
